# ===========================================================================
#  Build-context allowlist for the IsaacPX4 sim-stack image (Dockerfile).
#
#  The build context is this repo root (~130 GB). Docker ships the whole
#  context to the daemon BEFORE reading any COPY line, so we IGNORE EVERYTHING
#  and then re-include only the folders the Dockerfile actually COPYs -- and
#  trim the giant non-source blobs out of even those.
#
#  Net context after this file: a few GB, not 130 GB.
# ===========================================================================

# 1) Ignore everything by default.
*

# 2) PegasusSimulator (local fork) -> installed as an Isaac Sim extension.
!PegasusSimulator
#    ...but NOT the 29 GB Isaac assets zip, the 189 MB git history, or built docs.
PegasusSimulator/*.zip
PegasusSimulator/.git
PegasusSimulator/docs

# 3) PX4-Autopilot (local fork) -> SITL is COMPILED in a builder stage.
#    Keep the source + .git (PX4's build reads git for versioning/submodules);
#    drop the host's prebuilt Ubuntu-20.04 objects (we rebuild for 22.04).
!PX4-Autopilot
PX4-Autopilot/build

# 4) Out of ros2_ws, only the gimbal_stabilizer package (nested-allowlist ladder).
!ros2_ws
ros2_ws/*
!ros2_ws/src
ros2_ws/src/*
!ros2_ws/src/gimbal_stabilizer
ros2_ws/src/gimbal_stabilizer/.git

# 5) Sim worlds (USD, ~2.2 GB), tmux configs, env setup, QGroundControl.
!world
!tmux
!env
!QGroundControl.AppImage

# 6) Keep the build files themselves in context.
!Dockerfile
!.dockerignore
